WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.320
Is this you? You're working every day,

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.960
trying to keep up with the bills, never

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.600
quite breaking free of them? That was

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.825
actually me, too. I was right there with

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.040
you. But now, I've escaped the rat race.

00:00:09.825 --> 00:00:14.800
[music] It really comes down to seven

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.840
very easy habits that they never teach

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.600
you. And some of them are weird. Number

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.880
three might even piss some people off.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.440
But I'm not just going to tell you about

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.440
these habits. I actually want to help

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.800
you visually remember them to make

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:26.960
change. [music] This is all based on

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.880
neuroscience, so we will actually, by

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.840
the end of this video, change [music]

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.960
the way you think about money. All I can

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.400
do is talk from experience, and these

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.720
are the ones that made a difference for

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:40.120
me. Starting with the lizard brain

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:41.360
trick. So, can Do I lift him like this?

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.520
I don't know. I'm so freaked out to

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.240
squish him. Your brain is actively

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.640
working against you getting rich. And

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.160
most people have no idea it's happening.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.560
You know, you wake up, you crush a

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:53.240
morning routine, you send 40 emails, you

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.880
sit in three Zoom calls, and you color

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.480
code your calendar. But you feel like a

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.640
machine at the end of the day. Then you

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:57.720
look at your bank account,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.600
>> [music]

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.480
>> it's exactly where it was yesterday. And

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.640
that feeling sucks. There are two

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.400
problems, and both of them come from

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:08.320
what I call your lizard brain. So,

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.760
firstly, I like lizards. I like turtles.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.920
But I don't like your lizard brain

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.520
because it can't tell the difference

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.400
between sending an email and closing a

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:17.840
$10,000 deal. Neurologically, it

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.680
registers as task completed and fires

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.920
the same dopamine hit whether you

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.480
reorganize your desktop for 2 hours or

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.360
sign a contract. [music] So, it's this

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.880
like chemical good feeling that isn't

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.400
really productive at all. The other

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.400
problem with your lizard brain is that

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.011
it's lazy. Sorry, little guy. You see,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.720
it pulls you towards the easier thing

00:01:33.011 --> 00:01:36.920
[music] because the easier task gets

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.720
completed faster, which means more

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.200
dopamine sooner. So, your lizard brain

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.400
is trying to make you [music] feel good

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.240
right now, not make you rich. So, my

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.840
first habit, every morning, before you

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.840
pick up your phone, I want you to write

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:48.920
one line. [music]

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.680
The one task that, if done and done

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.200
only, it actually makes you money. So, I

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:53.920
want you to do that before touching

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.120
anything else. Because once you have

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.320
beaten this little guy, the next problem

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.600
is that most of what you're chasing is

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:02.240
entirely wrong. And so, I think we

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.560
should break down the next habit that

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:05.320
will make you throw your vision board in

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:08.280
the trash, but it might actually be a

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:09.800
good thing. Anti-goals before goals. So,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.320
most goal-setting advice tells you to

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.080
get clear on what you want, but Charlie

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.800
Munger thought that was the wrong place

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:16.720
to start, and I think he was right.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.680
Every time I'm setting financial targets

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.171
for something, whether this is my year,

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.040
a new business, a new investment,

00:02:20.171 --> 00:02:24.000
[music] I write the anti-goals first

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.080
before putting a single goal on the

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.360
page. Like, I don't [music] want to make

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.600
less than $20,000 a year, you know? I

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:31.760
don't want to work for 70 hours a week,

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.320
although I actually do. I don't want to

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.040
be financially dependent on another

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.440
person. I don't want to go into debt to

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.720
look wealthy, that's [music] true. And

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.800
then I write what I do want. Munger

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.520
calls this inversion, and he used it for

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.000
everything. So, instead of asking what

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:47.080
you do want, ask what you do [music] not

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.760
want. You probably skip this, and you go

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.040
straight to the dream board. But,

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:52.959
writing down the don't want [music] list

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.920
forces you to see something. Your wants

00:02:52.959 --> 00:02:57.640
and your don't wants are on a seesaw.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.959
Both can't sit at the top. If you don't

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.440
want to work 70 hours a week, and you

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:04.120
want to make $500,000 a year, those are

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:05.920
going to be in direct tension. So, you

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.280
might have to pick which one wins, at

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.952
least for a period, and let the other

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.000
one slide down. Most people never make

00:03:09.952 --> 00:03:12.200
>> [music]

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.720
>> that choice. So, here's your second

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.537
habit.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:14.959
I want you

00:03:14.537 --> 00:03:16.880
>> [music]

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:20.320
>> to take a piece of paper, line down the

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:22.560
middle. Left, what you want. Right, what

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:24.360
you don't want. Rank each side and see

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.560
where they conflict, and then choose

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:27.959
your seesaw winner. That one decision

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.400
tells you more about your financial

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:32.040
future than any business plan you've

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.120
written. Think about this. I want to

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:36.320
make over 500K a year, I don't want to

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.120
work more than 70 hours. Well, one of

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.800
these is going to have to go for a first

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:43.480
period, and that's okay. People, you

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:45.600
know, have lots of feelings about this,

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:47.640
but I think that if you choose the

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.959
things you don't want, it [music] makes

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.600
really clear what you are willing to do

00:03:50.959 --> 00:03:54.440
to get there. [music] Now, the next

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:56.440
habit is the one I get the most pushback

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.760
on. Some people call it elitist, but for

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:59.760
my [music] personal experience, it's

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:02.000
damn hard to argue with.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.360
I call it fire your friends. I'm from

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.440
Phoenix, [music] right? And I bet your

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.720
hometown has this, too. There's a great

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.280
bar there called Paddy's. But every time

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:12.360
I go back, the same characters are

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.080
there. The same conversations. It's kind

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:16.519
of like a record on repeat. Do you have

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:18.072
a place like that? If I had stayed, I'd

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:20.720
still probably be there. This is like

00:04:18.072 --> 00:04:22.160
[music] an anchor, your city. It becomes

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:23.967
something that holds you back. When

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.840
you're in your hometown, everyone

00:04:23.967 --> 00:04:28.480
[music] who knows you, they knew you

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:31.040
when you were 17. And so, they love you,

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:32.200
but that love is your 17-year-old self.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.480
And they've [music] anchored to it.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.680
These people around you, they'll pull

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:38.840
you without realizing it, toward [music]

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.320
the old version of yourself, the one

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.960
that feels safe and normal to them. And

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:44.120
so, when you leave, something different

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.560
happens, kind of magical. Nobody there

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.360
knows your old story. You get to be

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.400
someone your hometown hasn't ever met

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.000
before. And that blank slate lets you

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:53.120
build a different story before anyone

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.240
can correct you back to the old one. If

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.320
you want to do high-level things in

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.160
life, if you want to make a ton of

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:59.520
money, you have to be around people who

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:01.200
have already done those things. [music]

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.520
People who have done it, not people

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.240
thinking about it, or people who almost

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.760
did it, or people who want to talk

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.720
about the people even trying. This is

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:11.000
almost never located in the same zip

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.960
code where you grew up. And so, I want

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.480
you to constantly do one thing. If you

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:16.368
haven't moved from your hometown, it's

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:18.000
about time, even for a few months.

00:05:16.368 --> 00:05:20.400
[music] I want you to look around you

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.520
and say, "Where are my anchors today? Do

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.880
I live in a place that doesn't have

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:25.440
opportunity? Am I hanging out with

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:27.000
people who really haven't tried to

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.120
achieve much of anything? If they're

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.560
pushing you towards your goals, great.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:32.280
If not, it's time to go. It's time to go

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.440
somewhere new, you know, just long

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:35.440
enough that you have time to [music]

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:36.440
become someone different, right? Maybe

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:38.240
the person that you actually want to

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.960
become. Because you are allowed to be a

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:42.880
totally different human 1 year from now.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:44.600
This is actually what we are supposed to

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.160
do, but nobody wants you to do it. And

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:47.720
if you think Think this mentality, when

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.040
you apply it to money, It actually cuts

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.920
through more noise than any other

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:53.000
framework because you don't have to do

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:54.680
more things. You have to cut off the

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:56.760
things that are holding you back. This

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:58.480
next lesson I learned on Wall Street and

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.880
I never would have if I hadn't been

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:01.360
behind the curtain. So, I'm going to

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:03.320
share it with you. I call it killing

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.680
complexity. The financial industry

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.720
actually makes more money selling you

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.440
things that are complex than it ever

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.280
will selling you things that are simple.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.720
Someone wants to sell you a crypto

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:15.960
trading system that takes 3 hours a day

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:18.160
for a year in a master

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:21.560
financial freedom blueprint or more than

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:23.400
that, a 50-page legal [music] contract

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:25.200
that goes with your mutual fund report

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.400
that you can't even read and inside of

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.600
it they're slowly stealing all of your

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.384
money with something called basis

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:32.680
points. Why? Because when something is

00:06:30.384 --> 00:06:34.480
[music] complex, it feels like it's

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:36.320
smart. Like you're getting the real

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:38.600
thing. And complexity is [music]

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:41.480
profitable to sell to people searching

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:43.400
for a shortcut or who want to give the

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:45.480
reins to somebody [music] else. So,

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.960
every time I'm looking at making money,

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.440
I sort of apply one filter [music] to

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.320
it, which is what's the simplest version

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:52.680
of this that could work? Like and I ask

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:54.720
myself this question, [music] which is

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.880
what if it was easy? And it comes from

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.640
kind of a famous idea called Occam's

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.514
razor, which says the simplest

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.520
explanation is the most likely.

00:07:00.514 --> 00:07:02.720
>> [music]

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.919
>> And so, philosophers use it to dismantle

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:07.160
conspiracy theories, right? Birds are

00:07:04.919 --> 00:07:08.720
CIA agents. I don't know. I don't know.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.440
People think that the entire global

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.400
government is secretly coordinating a

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:14.080
world takeover. But have you ever met a

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.680
government employee? I mean, most of

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.080
these people they could barely keep

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.120
their own lights on. You think they're

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.280
going to orchestrate a global takeover?

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.120
I don't know. [music] They're probably

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:24.000
just really inefficient, highly

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.080
uncapable, overwhelmed people stuck in a

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:28.400
broken system. And so, if you apply the

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:30.000
same razor to money and you want to make

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.840
more of it, well then you negotiate a

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.720
raise. You get a better paying job. You

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:35.960
make more offers. You buy a small local

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:37.680
business. Those four things done by

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:40.000
someone with average intelligence like

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.520
me, maybe like you, those people as long

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.200
as you show [music] up, it turns out

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:45.520
they've produced more millionaires than

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:47.020
every complicated strategy combined. And

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.040
certainly way more

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.520
>> [music]

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.600
>> than if you just do what people on Wall

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.760
Street tell you to do.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:53.440
>> You finally found a broker on Wall

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:54.960
Street that you can trust.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:57.320
>> So, what's the habit there? At [music]

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:59.240
least for myself, every time you're

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:01.040
tempted by something complex, ask

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:02.480
yourself, what is the boring obvious

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:04.680
version of [music] this? Then do that

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:06.360
instead, because simplicity actually

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:07.325
removes a lot of your excuses. So, when

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.480
you don't know what to do,

00:08:07.325 --> 00:08:09.200
>> [music]

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:11.000
>> you know, you wait, you consume, you

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:13.360
plan, and then your bank account doesn't

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:16.400
actually move. So, I think you want to

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:17.600
actually simplify to move forward. The

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.840
thing is, you got to practice the

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:21.040
language of money every week. Most

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:23.280
people who want to get rich are

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:25.400
completely fluent in the theory and

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:27.600
completely illiterate in the practice.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:29.640
And that gap is going to be your issue.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:32.120
The language of money, this right here,

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:33.760
is actually really simple. You're going

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.440
to make offers, you're going to

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.440
